WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.230
Holly goes to extremes.

2
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:06.010
Its male and female flowers
grow on separate plants.

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.040
Hazel keeps its male and
female flowers separate,

4
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.580
on the same plant.

5
00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:15.190
In some flowers, the anthers shed their
pollen days before the stigma of the same

6
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.780
flower is ready.

7
00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.190
Most flowers have both
male and female parts.

8
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.570
So why do so many work hard to
avoid pollinating themselves?

9
00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:29.070
In this mission, you'll take a flower
apart and see what each part does.

10
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:34.140
Then you'll compare the different ways
flowers stop themselves from self-pollinating.

11
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:39.470
Your mission: explain why a flower with
both male and female parts works hard

12
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.170
not to pollinate itself.
